On 30 Mar 2010, at 00:51, A. PIEKARSKI wrote:

> How exactly will a change in the orthography change things?

A change in typography is not a change in orthography.

The underlying spelling is (and should be) the same in any case. The suggestion here is that some graphic variation may help learners or others to navigate a paragraph of text more easily, which can only be an aid to parsing.

